    "Ahmed Awadallah",
    "Ryen W. White",
    "Doug Burger",
    "Chi Wang"
  ],
  "year": 2023,
  "arxivId": "2308.08155",
  "abstract": "AutoGen is an open-source framework that enables developers to build large language model (LLM) applications using multi-agent conversations. It allows for customizable and conversable agents that can leverage LLMs, human inputs, and tools to accomplish tasks. AutoGen streamlines multi-agent workflows using conversation programming, a paradigm that simplifies the development of intricate applications. The framework has been demonstrated to achieve outstanding performance on various tasks, including math problem solving, retrieval-augmented code generation, and conversational chess.",
  "sections": [
    {
      "title": "The Core Idea",
      "content": "AutoGen is based on the idea of using <strong>multi-agent conversations</strong> to enable next-gen LLM applications. This approach allows for <strong>customizable and conversable agents</strong> that can leverage LLMs, human inputs, and tools to accomplish tasks. By using conversation programming, developers can streamline multi-agent workflows and create complex applications with ease.",
